pqn("D11","N11D",2011,22,"Foundations of Physical Education","Nature of physical education","Assertion (A): Physical education is an eclectic science.\nReason (R): Physical education borrows its principles from different sciences.\nIn the context of the above statements, which one of the following is correct?",["Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is the correct explanation of (A)", "Both (A) and (R) are true but (R) is not the correct explanation of (A)", "(A) is true, but (R) is false", "(A) is false, but (R) is true"],0,"Physical education is eclectic because it borrows its principles from several sciences.");
pqn("D11","N11D",2011,23,"Exercise Physiology","Muscular system","Assertion (A): Muscles are power houses that convert chemical energy into mechanical work.\nReason (R): Skeletal muscles are called voluntary muscles.\nIn the context of the above statements, which one of the following is correct?",["Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is the correct explanation of (A)", "Both (A) and (R) are true but (R) is not the correct explanation of (A)", "(A) is true, but (R) is false", "(A) is false, but (R) is true"],1,"Muscles convert chemical energy into mechanical work, and skeletal muscles are voluntary, but the second fact does not explain the first.");
